So on Windows: installer_user() must verify... the equivalent intent: install runs elevated/as the daemons' identity. Windows: no uid. Honest minimal port: cfg(unix) → uid check; cfg(windows) → no equivalent portable check without new deps → return Ok with a doc comment stating the invariant is enforced by the caller on Windows (NTFS ACLs / install context). That matches "layerfs-fuse Windows port" being experimental.

Now write the fix with edit tool. Need to read the file around 160-220 with proper line numbers to make precise edits. I have the sed output. Let me do the edits:

Edit 1 (lines ~164-169):
```rust
        if !directory.exists() {
            use std::os::unix::fs::DirBuilderExt;
            fs::DirBuilder::new()
                .mode(0o700)
                .create(directory)
                .map_err(text)?;
        }
```
→
```rust
        if !directory.exists() {
            #[cfg(unix)]
            {
                use std::os::unix::fs::DirBuilderExt;
                fs::DirBuilder::new()
                    .mode(0o700)
                    .create(directory)
                    .map_err(text)?;
            }
            #[cfg(not(unix))]
            fs::create_dir(directory).map_err(text)?;
        }
```
Wait — but `text` closure captured; fine.

Hmm, but there's a subtlety: on unix path, recursive create? Original used DirBuilder::new().create() (non-recursive). Keep identical on unix; Windows: fs::create_dir (non-recursive) matches.

Edit 2: installer_user():
```rust
/// Refuses an installer that is not the daemons' user.
fn installer_user() -> Result<(), String> {
    use std::os::unix::fs::MetadataExt;
    // the owner of /proc/self is this process's effective user
    let uid = fs::metadata("/proc/self")...
    if uid != DAEMON_UID { ... }
    Ok(())
}
```
→ gate the whole body:
```rust
/// Refuses an installer that is not the daemons' user.
#[cfg(unix)]
fn installer_user() -> Result<(), String> {
    ... unchanged ...
}

/// Windows has no portable uid equivalent; the daemons' identity is enforced by
/// the Store directory's ACLs (created by this user) instead of a uid check.
#[cfg(not(unix))]
fn installer_user() -> Result<(), String> {
    Ok(())
}
```
DAEMON_UID const used only by unix version → gate const too (else dead_code warning on windows; and on unix it's used). Actually `const DAEMON_UID: u32 = 0;` at line 24 — on Windows it'd be unused → warning not error. Gate it `#[cfg(unix)]`.

Need exact current line numbers. Let me read the file sections via read tool to get anchor lines. Lines 20-26 (const), 163-171 (dirbuilder), 205-219 (installer_user). Use read with ranges.

