Now write the write-path into context.rs. Big edit — add imports + Mutated helper + resolve_parent + callbacks (create, overwrite, write, set_file_size, rename, set_delete, cleanup, flush). FileContext gains pending_delete: Mutex<bool>.

Careful details:
- create: WinFsp passes `create_options: u32` — FILE_DIRECTORY_FILE = 0x1. mode: 0o644 files / 0o755 dirs. granted_access: FILE_ACCESS_RIGHTS (create signature has FILE_ACCESS_RIGHTS — yes create keeps it). open = Some(writable).
- After Published: file_info fill from stat; FileContext::new needs serial: stat.serial.
- write chunking: WRITE_WINDOW from layerfs_overlay (pub const). Split loop accumulating; each chunk a KernelMutation; final file_info from last stat or getattr.
- set_file_size: new_size with set_allocation_size flag: if allocation → just update file_info (no engine op) — allocation size is a hint; else Attributes{size: Some(new_size)}.
- rename: resolve old (parent,name) + new (parent,name); replace = replace_if_exists; destination_path = full component list of the new path (root-relative, including final name? "names the destination parent from the root" — from root to destination PARENT). Build from new_file_name split, excluding last component.
- Attributes input path: KernelInput::Attributes{mode,mtime,size} with handle → SetOpenAttributes. For set_file_size use handle-based (file owned). protected = serial, handle = context.handle.
- Write input: KernelInput::Write{offset, data, cached:false}; protected=serial; handle=Some(handle) — wait MutationRequest.handle + input Write → operation(file) requires Some(OpenFile) — the engine resolves the handle itself? `handle.filter(|_| by_handle)` passed into visit; the outcome's file is used. OK pass handle.
- The `open` field: only for Create replies.

Mutated extraction helper:
```rust
fn mutate(&self, protected: u64, handle: Option<u64>, input: MutationInput, open: Option<bool>) -> Result<Mutated, FspError> {
    let services = self.request_services()?;
    let Some(now) = crate::operations::write::time(std::time::SystemTime::now()) else { return Err(internal MSG) };
    let request = MutationRequest { mount: self.mount(), request: self.next_request(), protected, handle, input, open, now };
    let mutation = block_on(KernelMutation::perform(services, request)).map_err(|f| internal(&f.reason))?;
    let value = match mutation.value() {
        Ok(published) => Mutated { stat: published.stat.clone(), file: published.file, changed: published.changed },
        Err(declined) => return Err(map_declined(declined)),
    };
    let _ = block_on(mutation.replied());
    Ok(value)
}
```
map_declined: Refused(r)→map_refusal(r), NoSpace→STATUS_DISK_FULL, Contended→STATUS_RETRY (NTSTATUS constant exists? windows crate: STATUS_RETRY ✓), TargetTooLong→STATUS_NAME_TOO_LONG? Use STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_INVALID.

Also remove read_only_volume(true) from session params — it makes WinFsp itself refuse writes before reaching us! Must drop that. Update session.rs.

Also drop the mod.rs doc line "read-only increment" → update status text.

Let me now write all edits: context.rs (imports + FileContext + helpers + callbacks), session.rs (remove read_only_volume), mod.rs doc update. Write the new context.rs sections via edit on existing file. Sizeable — go.

