Found it: **`store/open.rs:23`: the SQLite Store backend hard-refuses anything except macOS/Linux**:
```rust
if config.backend != BackendSelection::Sqlite
    || !cfg!(any(target_os = "macos", target_os = "linux"))
{
    return Err(PersistenceError::BackendUnavailable);
}
```

That's an explicit platform gate in layerfs-persistence — the deepest "Windows not supported" point I've seen. Why would they gate it? Likely SQLite VFS requirements (WAL on network FS?), or untested. The bundled rusqlite compiles fine on Windows and SQLite works on NTFS — the gate is policy, not necessity (their WSL story avoids native Windows Store entirely).

Fix: extend the cfg to include windows — the honest experimental change. Check for other cfg(macos/linux) gates in persistence: grep `target_os = "macos"` across core to find all such gates that would block the Windows path.

